  "content": {
    "id": "p11-q8",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "8",
    "prompt": "By first identifying the domain and range of these functions, identify the domain and range of the inverse.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 3,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p11-q8-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$y=3x+4$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Original: domain all real $x$; range all real $y$. Inverse: domain all real $x$; range all real $y$.",
          "worked": "The linear function accepts every real input and takes every real output value.\n\nOriginal: $D=\\mathbb{R}$, $R=\\mathbb{R}$.\n\nInterchange the domain and range.\n\nInverse: $D=\\mathbb{R}$, $R=\\mathbb{R}$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 28
      },
      {
        "id": "p11-q8-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$y=\\sqrt{x}-3$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Original: $D=[0,\\infty)$, $R=[-3,\\infty)$. Inverse: $D=[-3,\\infty)$, $R=[0,\\infty)$.",
          "worked": "$x\\geq0$ is required for the square root. Since $\\sqrt{x}\\geq0$, the least output is $-3$.\n\nOriginal: $D=[0,\\infty)$, $R=[-3,\\infty)$.\n\nInterchange the domain and range.\n\nInverse: $D=[-3,\\infty)$, $R=[0,\\infty)$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 34
      },
      {
        "id": "p11-q8-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$y=x^2+1$, for $x\\geq0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Original: $D=[0,\\infty)$, $R=[1,\\infty)$. Inverse: $D=[1,\\infty)$, $R=[0,\\infty)$.",
          "worked": "The stated restriction gives $x\\geq0$. The minimum output is $1$, at $x=0$, and outputs increase without bound.\n\nOriginal: $D=[0,\\infty)$, $R=[1,\\infty)$.\n\nInterchange the domain and range.\n\nInverse: $D=[1,\\infty)$, $R=[0,\\infty)$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 34
      },
      {
        "id": "p11-q8-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$y=\\frac{3}{x}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Original: $D=\\mathbb{R}\\setminus\\{0\\}$, $R=\\mathbb{R}\\setminus\\{0\\}$. Inverse: $D=\\mathbb{R}\\setminus\\{0\\}$, $R=\\mathbb{R}\\setminus\\{0\\}$.",
          "worked": "The denominator excludes $x=0$. The output cannot equal $0$, and every other real output is possible.\n\nOriginal: $D=\\mathbb{R}\\setminus\\{0\\}$, $R=\\mathbb{R}\\setminus\\{0\\}$.\n\nInterchange the domain and range.\n\nInverse: $D=\\mathbb{R}\\setminus\\{0\\}$, $R=\\mathbb{R}\\setminus\\{0\\}$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 34
      },
      {
        "id": "p11-q8-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "$y=2^x$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Original: $D=\\mathbb{R}$, $R=(0,\\infty)$. Inverse: $D=(0,\\infty)$, $R=\\mathbb{R}$.",
          "worked": "$2^x$ is defined for every real $x$ and takes every positive output value.\n\nOriginal: $D=\\mathbb{R}$, $R=(0,\\infty)$.\n\nInterchange the domain and range.\n\nInverse: $D=(0,\\infty)$, $R=\\mathbb{R}$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 30
      },
      {
        "id": "p11-q8-f",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "f",
        "prompt": "$y=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x+2}}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Original: $D=(-2,\\infty)$, $R=(0,\\infty)$. Inverse: $D=(0,\\infty)$, $R=(-2,\\infty)$.",
          "worked": "The square root is in the denominator, so $x+2>0$, giving $x>-2$. Outputs are positive, approach $0$ as $x$ increases, and increase without bound as $x$ approaches $-2$ from above.\n\nOriginal: $D=(-2,\\infty)$, $R=(0,\\infty)$.\n\nInterchange the domain and range.\n\nInverse: $D=(0,\\infty)$, $R=(-2,\\infty)$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 38
      }
    ]
  },
